# The bare pass plus one test tool. Select it with `Run-PickleWsl.ps1 -DepMap wsl-deps.tools.map`;
# its report carries the pass name `tools`, this file's name without `wsl-deps.` and `.map`.
# One line per mod: packageId then its Workshop id, or `path:` for a folder in the collection.
#
# A run that names no map reads none at all: the runner sets PICKLE_DEPMAP=none, so a file called
# wsl-deps.map is never the default of the bare pass. That is why this one has a name of its own.
#
# The line below is not an optional mod. The mod under test is still the bare one, with no body
# retexture and nothing filling wornGraphicPath. It is a step package: 02-gear-tab.feature needs
# steps that open a pawn's inspect tabs, which the stock Pickle has not got. They exist twice, as
# RimWorks/Rimworld-Pickle#31, waiting for a merge, and as a PickleTools package that runs on the
# stock Pickle. The package is the route: a suite that took the modified Pickle through -PickleSrc
# would be testing a Pickle nobody else has.
#
# It has a pass of its own because the Gear tab is most useful in the bare pass: nothing is drawn
# there, so the game's own list of what a pawn wears is the only witness.
nelim.pickletools.inspecttabs   path:PickleTools/InspectTabs/Mod
